lass=\"bullet\">Use capital letters where necessary. </span>\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}]}], "id": 9, "stimuli_ids": []}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "RSLT", "questions": [{"responses": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0}, {"id": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "id": 10, "stimuli_ids": []}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "DWS", "questions": [{"responses": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn10le11ob06re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " \nResearch traditional uses of food.\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.\n", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "id": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le11ob06re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le11ob06re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn10le11ob06re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn10le11ob06re2img01.jpg", "text": "For many years, people have connected food to what happens to them. Long ago, one could find many interesting legends on food. People had wanted to believe these legends but they weren't scientifically proven to be true. Some are quite strange!\nMushrooms were often thought of as evil, perhaps because they were connected with fairies who were \u201cseen\" dancing on them. On the other hand, in Southeast Asia, finding mushrooms at the beginning of a trip meant that a person would be lucky. Travelers report that they had feared a difficult trip but when they saw a mushroom everything turned out to be fine.", "id": 1, "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn10le11ob06re2img02.jpg", "text": "In ancient Greece, beans were banned because people believed they brought bad dreams and madness. However, the ancient Egyptians believed beans had a soul and worshipped them.\nAs for healing powers of food, in Ireland people believed that potatoes had the ability to cure aches and pains. People would even walk around with potatoes in socks hung around their necks to avoid getting sore throats. They would rub potatoes on their skin to heal burns. People had expected potatoes to cure their ailments but it didn't always work.", "id": 2, "time": "31500"}, {"image": "engenn10le11ob06re2img03.jpg", "text": "Known to be of the oldest plants frequently used as a medicine, garlic has relieved ailments from coughs to fevers. If garlic is topically applied, it can help heal skin conditions like eczema and scabies, and prevent hair from going grey. Oddly enough, in the past, it was given to \u201chysterical\u201d girls because it was thought to calm them down if it was rubbed on their noses! People had hoped that garlic could improve emotional well-being but it wasn't effective.\n<br/> <br/>\nEven today, certain foods are believed to have healing powers. People eat cloves of raw garlic to prevent colds and flu, and honey to soothe a sore throat. Pharmaceutical companies that had expected to take over the healing business, haven't been able to beat some of these natural and ancient remedies.", "id": 3, "time": "59500"}]}}], "_data": []}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Culture, Myths, and Legends", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Folklore on Food", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 11, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Describe detailed facts about events or actions in work and social contexts, in written or spoken situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Placeholder", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Placeholder", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "x", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "x", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "x", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "x", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "x", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "xx", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le11ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Past Perfect to Describe Unfulfilled Plans", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use the Past Perfect tense to talk about unfulfilled events. These are things that you wanted to do, but for some reason they did not happen.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the Past Perfect with report verbs and with <span class=\"italic\">hope</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> intend</span>, <span class=\"italic\">expect </span>to talk about plans that have not yet been fulfilled. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use these types of constructions in speaking, you stress the word <span class=\"italic\">had</span>. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice reading these sentences aloud: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">had </span>hoped to talk to him but he was too busy to listen. </span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">had </span>thought of texting him but decided against it.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "People had wanted to believe these legends but they weren't scientifically proven to be true. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "People had expected potatoes to cure their ailments but it didn't always work.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Pharmaceutical companies had expected to take over the healing business, but they haven't been able to beat some of these natural and ancient remedies. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Travelers report that they had feared a difficult trip but when they saw a mushroom everything turned out to be fine.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "People had hoped that garlic could improve emotional well-being but it wasn't effective.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Scanning a Text", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Scanning is a reading skill. It involves looking at a text quickly in order to identify specific information.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use scanning when you want to find a specific name, date, time, statistic or fact without reading the whole text.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "These are some things to keep in mind in order to scan a text effectively:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><ol> <li>Keep the idea or image of what you are looking for in mind as you scan. This helps you to find it quickly.</li><li>Try to anticipate what form the information you want will appear in (nouns, verbs etc.).</li><li>Analyze the organization of the text before you scan.</li><li>Let your eyes quickly glance at several sentences at a time. </li><li>When you find the sentence with the detail you  want, read the entire sentence.</li></span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to ban", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200b\u200brefuse to \u200ballow something, \u200bespecially \u200bofficially", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In ancient Greece, beans were banned because people believed they brought bad dreams and madness.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le11ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about traditions, healing and illness.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "madness", "type": "name"}, {"content": "insanity", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Madness can be a problem among homeless people.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le11ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ailment", "type": "name"}, {"content": "medical problem", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: People had expected potatoes to cure their ailments but it didn't always work.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le11ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to cure", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make someone with an \u200billness \u200bhealthy again", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In Ireland people believed that potatoes had the ability to cure aches and pains.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le11ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "eczema", "type": "name"}, {"content": "\u200bskin \u200bcondition in which \u200bareas of the \u200bskin \u200bbecome \u200bred, \u200brough, and \u200bsore ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If garlic is topically applied, it can help heal skin conditions like eczema and scabies. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le11ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to soothe", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make a \u200bpart of the \u200bbody less \u200bpainful", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: People eat cloves of raw garlic to prevent colds and flu, and honey to soothe a sore throat. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le11ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pharmaceutical", "type": "name"}, {"content": "\u200brelating to the \u200bproduction of \u200bmedicines", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Pharmaceutical companies had expected to take over the healing business, but they haven't been able to beat some of these natural and ancient remedies. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le11ob06aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to prevent", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to stop something from happening", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Garlic has been applied externally to prevent hair from going grey.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le11ob06aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "On the Internet, research traditional uses of food.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a list of some traditional uses of food from around the world.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose one and do more research.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a poster that shows the food that you chose, its traditional uses and its current uses, if any.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your poster and research to your class or group.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research traditional uses of food.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make a poster to show the traditional uses of food.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present my poster to a group.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present my research findings to a group.", "type": "text"}]}]}